# =============================================================================
# lsdtt3 .gitignore
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build and output directories
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# build_*/ as well as build/: out-of-tree build directories get suffixed names
# (build_ws1, build_gpu, build_asan) and a bare `build/` catches none of them.
# A `git add -A` in a tree with one of these in it stages a couple of thousand
# object files, and that is how it is normally noticed.
build/
build_*/
bin/
for_elm/
site/
.ccls-cache/

# CTest scratch: `ctest` writes Testing/Temporary/ (LastTest.log and friends)
# into whatever directory it is run from, which includes the repository root.
Testing/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compiled object files and static libraries
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CUDA compiled objects
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.cubin
*.ptx

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CMake generated files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
CMakeScripts/
cmake_install.cmake
install_manifest.txt
compile_commands.json
CTestTestfile.cmake
_deps/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Apptainer / Singularity container images
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.sif
*.simg

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and IDE files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# VS Code
.vscode/

# Visual Studio
.vs/

# CLion / JetBrains
.idea/
cmake-build-*/

# Vim
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Emacs
\#*\#
.\#*

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Windows
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*.exe
*.dll

# Packaged artifacts
*.zip

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python (scripts, notebooks, test helpers)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
dist/
*.ipynb_checkpoints/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Parameter files with local paths — keep example files, ignore run-specific ones
# Add your own run parameter files here if needed, e.g.:
# my_local_run.driver
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Output rasters — GeoTIFF and related formats
# Uncomment if you do not want to track any output rasters in the repo.
# Leave commented if you want to track small test rasters in tests/data/.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# *.tif
# *.tiff
# *.vrt

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Benchmark DEM fixtures
#
# Fetched at test time from Copernicus GLO-30, never committed
# (see docs/developer_notes/testing_and_benchmarking.md).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
tests/data/dem_cache/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# pixi environments (pixi.toml and pixi.lock ARE tracked)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pixi/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Benchmark campaign output (tests/scripts/run_benchmark_suite.py)
#
# Each run writes a self-contained, timestamped directory. These are machine-
# and moment-specific measurements, not source: committing them would grow the
# repository without making any result more reproducible, since the campaign
# already records the git SHA, hardware and fixture hashes needed to repeat it.
# Tar the directory and attach it to wherever the numbers are published.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
benchmark_campaigns/

# Slurm job logs written by tests/scripts/slurm_benchmark.sbatch.
slurm_logs/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Planning documents
#
# docs/plan_docs/ holds working plans - they are drafted, revised and abandoned
# during a piece of work and are not the durable record. What survives a plan
# goes into docs/ proper (see docs/developer_notes/testing_and_benchmarking.md for the pattern:
# the committed document is the record, the plan is the scaffolding). A
# committed file must never cite a plan doc, because the plan may not exist.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/plan_docs/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LaTeX technical notes
#
# docs/tex_technical/ holds standalone LaTeX notes written for papers, not for
# the mkdocs site (mkdocs.yml already excludes the directory from the build).
# They are drafts carried alongside the code rather than part of the published
# documentation, so they are not tracked here.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/tex_technical/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local git identity mapping
#
# .mailmap canonicalises author names and addresses in git history. It is kept
# local rather than committed: it reflects one person's view of who is who,
# including addresses that need not be published in the repository.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.mailmap

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run output written into the repository root
#
# Analysis runs driven from the repo root drop their rasters, tables and vectors
# beside the source. They are outputs of a particular run on a particular DEM,
# not fixtures: test fixtures live under tests/data/ and are added deliberately.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
internal_drainage_detect_output/
point_input_test_output/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent tooling and scratch
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/
src/resume_claude.txt

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Debian packaging build output
#
# The package definition itself IS committed: debian/control, debian/rules,
# debian/changelog, debian/source/format and debian/smoke-test.sh. Everything
# listed below is produced by dpkg-buildpackage - debhelper's out-of-tree CMake
# build directory, the staged package root, debhelper's own bookkeeping, and
# the built artefacts. Note that dpkg writes the .deb one level ABOVE the
# source tree, so the artefact patterns here are belt-and-braces.
#
# The package cannot be built on a /mnt/c (NTFS) path: every file reports mode
# 777 there and dpkg-deb rejects a control directory more permissive than 0775.
# Build from a Linux-native directory. See docs/developer_notes/debian_packaging.md
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
obj-*/
debian/lsdtt3/
debian/.debhelper/
debian/files
debian/*.substvars
debian/*.debhelper.log
debian/debhelper-build-stamp
*.deb
*.ddeb
*.buildinfo
*.changes

# Help / parameter-echo files from running the param-deprecation test child by hand
/dep_parser_*
